# Project Rules

## Comments
- Do not add comments everywhere in the code.
- Each file should have at most one short, brief comment summarizing what it does.
- Each service should have one comment describing what the whole service does.
- Comments must be written in plain, simple language — no buzzwords or jargon.
- Any new developer should be able to read the comment and immediately understand the purpose, without needing extra context.

## Folder Structure
- Follow proper, consistent folder structure across the project.
- Group related files together (e.g. by feature or domain), don't scatter related logic across unrelated folders.

## Constants & Types
- All constants must be defined in a dedicated `constants` file only.
- All types/interfaces must be defined in a dedicated `types` file only.
- Do not define constants or types inline inside other files.
- Always export constants and types from their respective files and import them where needed.